Start a remote workspace from the settings the page read for it.

For a remote folder, the configuration a window starts with holds the folder's
own settings only as the copy its last load cached. A folder opened for the
first time has no such copy, so until its .vscode/settings.json has been read
through the remote file system, which waits for that provider to register and
then for the read, the window runs on the user's settings alone. On an Android
emulator that read ended 8.5 to 20.6 s into the load. Whatever read the
configuration in that time got the user's values, the theme service first of
all: a folder whose settings name Light Modern under a user theme of Dark
Modern showed Dark Modern from the start of the load until the file had been
read. A remote workspace file is held the same way, folders included.

The page that hosts the workbench, which VSCodroid adds a script to, reads the
folder's settings file, or the workspace file, over HTTP as it loads, before
the workbench starts, and hands its text over in the new construction option
initialWorkspaceSettings: null where there is no such file, nothing where the
read failed. The configuration of the window's first load starts from that
text in place of the cached copy: the folder's settings, with the cached tasks,
launch and MCP configurations kept, since the page reads the settings file
alone; or the whole workspace file. The swap to the file system and the read
through it are unchanged, so the read still ends with the change event for
whatever differs, which is nothing unless the file changed in between. Any
later load, a folder of a multi-root workspace, and an embedder that does not
pass the option are as before.

The option names the workspace by nothing but the window it is given to, so
the workspace service drops it once its first initialization is done.

This rests on 0026. The folder's settings from the page live in the cached
configuration, which the file based one replaces as soon as the provider
registers and before it has read anything; without 0026 the reparse that every
change to the default configuration makes, as the extensions register, would
reparse the empty replacement and drop them until the read ends.

For patches/fingerprints.txt: the option is read as
`environmentService.options?.initialWorkspaceSettings`, and property names
survive this bundle, so that read is the token the row matches. Reading the
option anywhere else, or into a local first, deletes it; move the row with it.

